# {{name}} Admin example

Generated opt-in source for `{{id}}`. Review and format before explicit source
synchronization/install/enable. Generation does not change registry or grants.
The module keeps its existing independent version; assess its release and install
history before delivering these source/settings changes to existing installations.

The working example normalizes text without storing user submissions. Its owning
`{{namespace}}\Contracts\{{name}}Tools::normalize(string $text): string` is API
1.0.0; resolve it through ModuleApis for `{{id}}`, requiring native permission
`{{id}}.{{key}}.use`. It works without Admin. The generated handler validates
160-character text and refuses controls. No domain record, UUID or Audit success
is invented for a calculation. Do not turn this adapter into a persisted Save
without owning validation, record Policies, revisions, transaction and Audit.

Admin discovers the declared `{{key}}` page in Tools, generated form/action,
read-only single-row table, widget and owned summary contribution. The default
section component is `{{id}}.{{key}}_section`, discovered by the existing build
registry; no dynamic import path is accepted from HTTP. The widget has unknown
observation freshness: reading a setting is not a health observation. The stateless
table row has no public ID and cannot be selected as a durable entity.

Module settings expose `{{key}}_text` as an immediate default, separately from
calculation results. This example does not expose settings editing. For an administrator editor, declare
a dedicated module-owned page using the named snapshot adapter and public
AdminSettingsPage from docs/runa/handbook/modules/admin/settings-snapshots.md.
Retain owning grants, validation, publication revisions and Audit; settings do not
join aggregate Save.
The source-owned settings provider is singular. Existing provider owners must
merge definitions deliberately instead of generating a second provider.

To contribute to a foreign host, change the explicit contribution host in
`{{name}}Management`, retain owned section/binding/component/permissions and add
the owning module as an optional manifest dependency. Host absence/denial must
not prevent the business API from working. Never add a required Admin dependency.

Application-owned partial/full replacements compose `@/runa/admin` public props,
controllers and AdminPresentationProvider. Keep one shared Auth session shell;
do not copy security or import private adapters. See
`docs/runa/handbook/modules/admin/examples.md` for working consumer patterns,
registration, atomic participation, testing and limitations.

Run the generated owning test using `{{test_command}}`. Add application-specific
record-policy, denial, dirty-draft, rollback and rendered replacement scenarios
when extending the example. Delivery/update must preserve these application files.


The source provider implements ManagementReadPlanProvider (Framework API ^1.1.0).
It declares one normalize invocation for each record/page/widget read. If you add
nested or repeated health-sensitive API calls, update its exact input-based plan
and targets. Health preparation runs before the locked Admin read; grants, proof,
record Policies and current source/expiry still apply inside it. Follow
`docs/runa/handbook/modules/admin/declarations.md#read-health-plans`.
